From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] contour: load private Wayland target from public component

License: Apache-2.0
Upstream-Status: downstream-only
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

Qt 6.5's Wayland development package exports both Qt6::WaylandClient and
Qt6::WaylandClientPrivate from Qt6WaylandClientConfig.cmake.  It does not ship
a separate Qt6WaylandClientPrivateConfig.cmake, so asking Qt's component
loader for WaylandClientPrivate makes an otherwise complete package fail.

Load the public WaylandClient component, which imports both targets, and keep
linking the private target exactly as before.  The protocol generator and all
Wayland functionality remain enabled.

Remove this patch when upstream no longer requests WaylandClientPrivate as a
separate Qt component, or when the target distribution provides its separate
component configuration.

---
 src/contour/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/contour/CMakeLists.txt b/src/contour/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/contour/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/contour/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@ if(CONTOUR_FRONTEND_GUI)
     endif()
 
     if(LINUX AND CONTOUR_WAYLAND)
-        find_package(Qt6 COMPONENTS WaylandClient WaylandClientPrivate)
+        find_package(Qt6 COMPONENTS WaylandClient REQUIRED)
         target_compile_definitions(contour PRIVATE CONTOUR_WAYLAND)
         target_link_libraries(contour PRIVATE Qt6::WaylandClient Qt6::WaylandClientPrivate)
         qt6_generate_wayland_protocol_client_sources(contour FILES "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/protocols/blur.xml")
